==Russian==

===Etymology===
'''Иван''', from Old Russian [[Иваннъ]], from Old Russian, Old Slavonic [[Иоаннъ]], from New Testament Greek {{m|grc|Ἰωάννης}}, from Hebrew {{m|he|יוֹחָנָן|tr=[[Johanan|Jōħānān]]}}, perhaps from a former {{m|he|יְהוֹחָנָן|tr=Yehochanan}} {{IPAchar|J<sup>ə</sup>hôħānān}}, meaning "God is gracious".

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|Ива́н}}
* {{audio|Ru-Иван.ogg|Audio|lang=ru}}

===Proper noun===
{{ru-proper noun+|Ива́н|a=an|n=both}}

# {{given name|male|lang=ru}}, [[Ivan]], equivalent to [[John]].
# [[India]] (''I'' in the [[Appendix:Russian phonetic alphabet|ICAO]] spelling alphabet)
# {{lb|ru|pejorative|rare}} {{clipping of|lang=ru|Иван-дурак}} {{wiki|ru:Иван-дурак}}

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-table|Ива́н|a=an}}

